# Annotation-app reviewer output (JSONL data). NOT the review reports in
# docs/re-implementation-sep/reviews/ - a bare `reviews` pattern here silently
# untracked every phase review report from Phase 0 onward, while the phase
# summaries linked to them as though they were in the repository.
templates_annotation/annotation_app/reviews/
iaa_results
ai_human_alignment_results
Evaluation Results EngChain FINAL
error_analysis_samples
ai_assisted_quality_assurance/ai_tribunal_results
validation/
# pilot_new_branches/ is the September staging area from BUILDING the civil and
# industrial branches - large reference PDFs, draft templates, a testset preview.
# It is not the evaluation pilot; it held only those two branches because those
# were the two being built. Superseded by data/templates/branches/ (all five) and
# docs/references/. Kept locally, not committed, except the README that says so.
pilot_new_branches/*
!pilot_new_branches/README.md

# evaluator_pilot_17092026/ is the evaluation pilot, and its code and frozen slice ARE
# committed. The freeze is the record that 300 annotated traces were labelled
# against a specific set of items: untracked, it cannot be verified later, which
# is the one thing a freeze is for. Only the model outputs are held back, matching
# how inference_results/ is treated above.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/traces/
# Evaluator outputs, like traces, are produced data. The venv holds torch and the
# scorer stack for E0, isolated so the pilot does not change the system Python.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/scores/
evaluator_pilot_17092026/.venv/

scratch/

# docs/references: large source binaries are NOT committed. MANIFEST.json records
# each one's URL and SHA-256, and fetch_references.py re-acquires and verifies
# them on any checkout. The small text/TSV/HTML/JSON sources ARE committed.
docs/references/**/*.pdf
docs/references/**/*.zip
docs/references/**/*.xlsx

# Stage 3 annotation: tasks are rebuilt by build_tasks.py, labels are produced data
# (and labels_simulated is synthetic). The scripts, the guide and its PDF are committed.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/annotation/tasks/
evaluator_pilot_17092026/annotation/labels/
evaluator_pilot_17092026/annotation/labels_simulated/
evaluator_pilot_17092026/annotation/dist/

# The experts' filled labels stay local only; they are never committed.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/experts_filled_labels/

# Mining output, rebuilt by hard_case_pool.py.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/analysis/out/

# The full run's item pool and its master seed stay local until publication (D-114):
# the templates are public, so the seed or the text would publish the items.
# Committed instead: full_run_28092026/manifest.jsonl (hashes only) and FREEZE.json.
full_run_28092026/pool/
full_run_28092026/SEED.secret

# The full run's traces restate the pool's questions, so they stay local like the pool.
full_run_28092026/traces/

# The full run's score store holds values derived from the private pool and traces.
full_run_28092026/scores/

# The paraphrases restate private items; their text, the experts' kits and returns stay local (D-141).
# Committed instead: paraphrase/manifest.jsonl (hashes only), PARAPHRASE.md and PARAPHRASE_REVIEW.md.
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/attempts*.jsonl
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/pool.jsonl
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/tasks/
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/dist/
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/returned/
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/experts_filled_paraphrases/
full_run_28092026/paraphrase/accepted.json

# The experts' reading request (D-172): the kits hold pool text and the keyfile, the returns the experts' labels.
# Committed instead: expert_kits.py, reading_app.py, EXPERT_READING_GUIDE.md and EXPERT_REQUEST.md (counts).
full_run_28092026/expert_request/

# The open-book arm (C4, D-183): the modified questions restate pool text and stay local; the manifest (hashes) is committed.
full_run_28092026/openbook/items.jsonl
full_run_28092026/openbook/items2.jsonl

# docs/related_work_oct2026: the PDFs of cited and candidate papers and their extracted text
# are NOT committed (size, copyright). papers.json, candidates/*.json, MANIFEST.json and
# fetch_papers.py re-acquire and verify them on any checkout.
docs/related_work_oct2026/papers/
docs/related_work_oct2026/text/
docs/related_work_oct2026/bib_raw/

# civil_industrial_sources/ holds the reference set used by the colleague who wrote the civil and
# industrial templates (received 2026-10-03): the public-domain handbooks (the same files docs/references/
# holds), copyrighted textbooks and their extracted text, and the manifest. Never committed.
civil_industrial_sources/
